From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 06:32:54 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] qosify: name a long device's ifb after its own name

For a device name of 12 to 15 characters, qosify takes the tail of its
ifb's name from before the name: undefined behavior, and an ifb named
after whatever precedes the name in memory. qosify-status derives the
ifb's name in a way of its own, which disagrees with the daemon's for
those lengths.

Carry the qosify patch that takes the name's last nine characters, as
the code means to, and reports each interface's ifb in its status, and
have qosify-status show that device. It is meant for qosify upstream.

Signed-off-by: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 package/network/config/qosify/Makefile        |  2 +-
 .../network/config/qosify/files/qosify-status |  6 +--
 ...long-device-s-ifb-after-its-own-name.patch | 47 +++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 51 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 package/network/config/qosify/patches/104-interface-name-a-long-device-s-ifb-after-its-own-name.patch

diff --git a/package/network/config/qosify/Makefile b/package/network/config/qosify/Makefile
index 9d4383e..34c5909 100644
--- a/package/network/config/qosify/Makefile
+++ b/package/network/config/qosify/Makefile
@@ -14,7 +14,7 @@ PKG_SOURCE_PROTO:=git
 PKG_SOURCE_DATE:=2026-06-22
 PKG_SOURCE_VERSION:=beeb87ec1f16aaf5d99ff8060c2455971d9d400e
 PKG_MIRROR_HASH:=c9ef0ad68daedb7e18e4959884a40cc0c64849dbd17bf6fdadeed8bdd8d49358
-PKG_RELEASE:=5
+PKG_RELEASE:=6
 
 PKG_LICENSE:=GPL-2.0
 PKG_MAINTAINER:=Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
diff --git a/package/network/config/qosify/files/qosify-status b/package/network/config/qosify/files/qosify-status
index dc58232..0ff60d1 100644
--- a/package/network/config/qosify/files/qosify-status
+++ b/package/network/config/qosify/files/qosify-status
@@ -7,7 +7,7 @@ dev_status() {
 }
 
 common_status() {
-	json_get_vars ifname ingress egress
+	json_get_vars ifname ingress egress ifb
 
 	[ -n "$ifname" ] || return
 
@@ -15,9 +15,9 @@ common_status() {
 		echo "egress status:"
 		dev_status "$ifname"
 	}
-	[ "$ingress" -gt 0 ] && {
+	[ -n "$ifb" ] && {
 		echo "ingress status:"
-		dev_status "$(printf %.16s "ifb-$ifname")"
+		dev_status "$ifb"
 	}
 }
 
diff --git a/package/network/config/qosify/patches/104-interface-name-a-long-device-s-ifb-after-its-own-name.patch b/package/network/config/qosify/patches/104-interface-name-a-long-device-s-ifb-after-its-own-name.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..ddd24c3
--- /dev/null
+++ b/package/network/config/qosify/patches/104-interface-name-a-long-device-s-ifb-after-its-own-name.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,47 @@
+From: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
+Subject: [PATCH] interface: name a long device's ifb after its own name
+
+For a device name of 12 to 15 characters, interface_ifb_name() keeps the
+name's first two characters and means to add its last nine. It takes
+them from iface->ifname + len - (IFNAMSIZ + 6) - 1, which is 8 to 11
+characters before the name: undefined behavior, and an ifb named after
+whatever precedes the name in memory.
+
+Take the tail at len - (IFNAMSIZ - 7), the last nine characters. With
+"ifb-" and the first two, they make the fifteen that an interface name
+holds.
+
+Report each active interface's ifb in its status, as "ifb", so that
+qosify-status can show the device the daemon created. It derives a name
+of its own today, which disagrees with the daemon's for such lengths.
+
+Signed-off-by: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
+---
+ interface.c | 5 ++++-
+ 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
+
+diff --git a/interface.c b/interface.c
+index d5ffbab..b278798 100644
+--- a/interface.c
++++ b/interface.c
+@@ -202,9 +202,10 @@ interface_ifb_name(struct qosify_iface *iface)
+ 		return ifname;
+ 	}
+ 
++	/* The name's first two characters and its last nine */
+ 	ifname[4] = iface->ifname[0];
+ 	ifname[5] = iface->ifname[1];
+-	snprintf(ifname + 6, IFNAMSIZ - 6, "%s", iface->ifname + len - (IFNAMSIZ + 6) - 1);
++	snprintf(ifname + 6, IFNAMSIZ - 6, "%s", iface->ifname + len - (IFNAMSIZ - 7));
+ 
+ 	return ifname;
+ }
+@@ -637,6 +638,8 @@ __qosify_iface_status(struct blob_buf *b, struct qosify_iface *iface)
+ 		blobmsg_add_string(b, "ifname", iface->ifname);
+ 	blobmsg_add_u8(b, "egress", iface->config.egress);
+ 	blobmsg_add_u8(b, "ingress", iface->config.ingress);
++	if (iface->active && iface->config.ingress)
++		blobmsg_add_string(b, "ifb", interface_ifb_name(iface));
+ 	blobmsg_close_table(b, c);
+ 
+ }
